## Project Overview

This repository documents the design and implementation of an isolated penetration testing laboratory built using Oracle VirtualBox.

The project demonstrates the complete penetration testing lifecycle, including:

- Lab Design
- Network Reconnaissance
- Service Enumeration
- Vulnerability Assessment
- Social Engineering
- Security Recommendations

---

# Documentation

| Section | Description |
|---------|-------------|
| [01 - Lab Setup](docs/01-lab-setup.md) | Configure the virtual penetration testing environment |
| [02 - Reconnaissance & Host Discovery](docs/02-reconnaissance-and-host-discovery.md) | Discover active hosts and services |
| [03 - Service Enumeration & Vulnerability Assessment](docs/03-service-enumeration-and-vulnerability-assessment.md) | Identify services and assess potential vulnerabilities |
| [04 - Social Engineering Assessment](docs/04-social-engineering-assessment.md) | Credential harvesting simulation using SET |
| [05 - Security Recommendations](docs/05-security-recommendations.md) | Recommendations based on assessment findings |

